        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la cotta",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la cotta — \"crush (on someone)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A quindici anni avevo una cotta per un compagno di classe. At fifteen I had a crush on a classmate."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Prendersi una cotta per qualcuno — to get a crush on someone. Informal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cotta is the feminine past participle of cuocere \"to cook\", from Latin coquere (Lewis & Short): someone cotto is cooked through with love."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
